        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Settings: add unified usage and spend dashboard",
        "body": "## Summary\n- Add a dedicated **Usage & Spend** pane to Settings for every enabled AI subscription.\n- Lead with aggregate estimated spend and tracked tokens, then rank subscriptions and actual model usage in separate sections.\n- Keep the existing native CodexBar visual language while borrowing the scanability of model-ranking surfaces: aligned totals, provider color and icon cues, relative bars, and a secondary daily spend chart.\n- Derive everything locally from existing cost-history snapshots; missing pricing remains explicitly unavailable instead of being reported as zero.\n\n## Scope\nThis PR only adds the unified Settings dashboard. The shareable social card is intentionally isolated in #2112.\n\n## Privacy and data semantics\n- No upload, public link, or backend is introduced.\n- Model rankings come from real `modelBreakdowns` in the selected 7- or 30-day window.\n- Providers without priced local history stay visible as configured subscriptions, but do not dilute spend totals.\n\n## Design sign-off\nThis is a new Settings surface, so the PR is intentionally a draft for product/design sign-off under `VISION.md`. The information hierarchy is intentionally spend-first: totals, subscriptions, models, then trend.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `swift build`\n- [x] `swift test --filter UnifiedSpendDashboardModelTests`\n- [x] `make check`\n- [ ] Full sharded suite in CI\n\n## Visual QA\n- Verified with a local SwiftUI render using real aggregate history.\n- The draft does not attach that render because it contains private spend data; a sanitized screenshot can be added before marking ready.\n",
